  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At the mountain stone tombstones of fallen Tie clansmen, an aged voice startles Tie Xuan Zhi, then a wizened hand on his shoulder names him and asks him to compose himself. Tie Xuan Zhi blurts out old clan leader; the old man says he has already abdicated, is not an elder now, and that the name Tie Mu Bai was meant to be used. He stands before the steles and tells Tie Ruo Nan that Tie clansmen are buried where they die, that dying on the battlefield is their greatest honor, and that her father Tie Xue Leng was the same.",
      "chapters": [
        369
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_xuan_zhi",
        "char_tie_ruo_nan",
        "char_tie_xue_leng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is a wizened old man. Vicissitudes of life are reflected in his eyes.",
      "chapters": [
        369
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tie Ruo Nan recognizes him as rank five peak stage, Tie clan’s previous generation clan leader, who once moved unhindered in Southern Border and pressed Wu clan, Shang clan, and other great clans while he reigned. He asks if she wants to uphold justice, then begins imparting metal path, the Gu path Tie clan Gu Masters use to stand on top of Southern Border.",
      "chapters": [
        370
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "glory-of-tie-clan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_ruo_nan",
        "fac_tie_clan",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "fac_shang_clan",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Eight days later he stands at the peak of San Cha mountain and suppresses the combined power of Yi Huo, Kong Ri Tian, Long Qing Tian, Yi Chong, and Wu Shen Tong. Talk on the mountain names him the glory of Tie clan and an old generation expert still alive. Divine Thief Lu Zuan Feng’s infiltration of Demonic Suppression Tower disturbed his closed cultivation; he struck and badly wounded that rank five thief, then chose to visit San Cha mountain after Tie Ba Xiu’s death angered Tie clan higher-ups. From the peak he announces that from that day no demonic Gu Master may enter three kings inheritance, sweeps demonic Gu Masters from the mountain by force of presence, and later holds a banquet for righteous path Gu Masters. He praises Fang Yuan as little beast king while warning against letting hatred deceive wisdom, assigns Fang Zheng as Tie Ruo Nan’s mission, and toasts the glory of righteousness.",
      "chapters": [
        370
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "glory-of-tie-clan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "char_yi_huo",
        "char_kong_ri_tian",
        "char_long_qing_tian",
        "char_yi_chong",
        "char_wu_shen_tong",
        "char_lu_zuan_feng",
        "char_tie_ba_xiu",
        "sys_demonic_path",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_fang_zheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Chou Jiu ascends San Cha mountain, Tie Mu Bai invites him earnestly and the two drink happily in a banquet.",
      "chapters": [
        375
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "glory-of-tie-clan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chou_jiu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under his influence three kings inheritance becomes a righteous path garden of exploration until Wu Gui, also rank five peak stage and named his lifetime rival, arrives in dark clouds. Talk places Wu Gui’s hatred in a ruined rank six breakthrough spoiled by a younger Tie Mu Bai, and the two fight inside the clouds with Tie Mu Bai holding the early advantage. Ku Mo then joins, and the fight becomes two demonic path rank five peak stage Gu Masters against him.",
      "chapters": [
        372
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rival-fight-above-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wu_gui",
        "char_ku_mo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the open clash he wears rank four golden coat Gu as golden chainmail and rank four golden aurora Gu as a layer of gold-red flight light covering his whole body, and his rank five turn gold Gu turns what it hits into lifeless golden sculpture. Fang Yuan judges that Tie clan resources should give him at least three rank five Gu, and that he will not show every trump card, so the battle has neither a clear winner nor loser from the start.",
      "chapters": [
        373
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rival-fight-above-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_turn_gold_gu",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "While Tie Mu Bai explores the inheritance, Fang Yuan appears before him with land spirit help, summons a rock crocodile phantom, and smashes his head with the crocodile’s tail.",
      "chapters": [
        378
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan enters the headless corpse’s aperture: crystal purple primeval essence at rank five peak stage, ninety-eight percent full, with vital Gu turn gold Gu, liquid metal Gu, and vajra stare Gu as rank five worms, plus four rank four metal path Gu including golden dragon Gu, golden breeze Gu, golden coat Gu, and golden aurora Gu. Beast strength placenta Gu swallows the aperture and raises second aperture Gu aptitude to forty percent.",
      "chapters": [
        379
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_vital_gu",
        "gu_liquid_metal_gu",
        "gu_beast_strength_placenta_gu",
        "gu_second_aperture_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later places only Tie Mu Bai, Ku Mo, and Wu Gui at rank five peak stage among five rank five Gu Masters on San Cha mountain, with Tie Mu Bai’s foundation deepest from Tie clan resources.",
      "chapters": [
        381
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later activates golden breeze Gu obtained from Tie Mu Bai: a rank four healing Gu that shows only rank three efficiency in Northern Plains, still treated as top quality.",
      "chapters": [
        428
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reduced-effect-in-northern-plains",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_golden_breeze_gu",
        "sys_healing_gu",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    }
  ],
